Find the smallest non-negative integer x that satisfies the following system of congruences:
x \equiv 11 \pmod{36}
x \equiv 7 \pmod{40}
x \equiv 32 \pmod{75}

Consider the function f: R^2 -> R defined by\nf(x, y) = 
\begin{cases} 
\frac{x^3 + y^3}{x^2 + y^2} & \text{if } (x, y) \neq (0, 0) \\
0 & \text{if } (x, y) = (0, 0)
\end{cases}
\nCalculate the partial derivative of f with respect to x at the point (0, 0).
